  "locus": "Theses in quibus exponitur An & quatenus homo per Christi gratiam Legem implere possit, & Dei mandata servare, XIX-XXXIII (even the good works of the regenerate fall short of the law's exactness, as Paul confesses (Phil. 3:12-14); objection from the 'perfect' of Phil. 3:15, 1 Cor. 2:6, Noah (Gen. 6:9), Job (Job 1:8; 2:3) and David (Psalm 18); answered by absolute versus comparative perfection (1 Cor. 3:1) and by perfection of degrees versus perfection of parts; the three marks of true and sincere obedience (inward, entire, persevering), which the regenerate have; Tham/thamim means integrity (Eph. 4:24); the orthodox position stated; Roman controversialists (Bellarmine, Becanus, Vasquez) misstate the question; Protestant witnesses: Pareus, Ames, Davenant on the Tridentine canon, and Robert Baron of Aberdeen on evangelical epieikeia (Heb. 12:14)).",
